     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10012\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the assessor of the town of Brookha-\nven, county of Suffolk, to accept an application for a real property tax\nexemption from Chabad at Stony Brook, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow the town of Brookhaven to accept an application for a retro-ac-\ntive property tax exemption from the Chabad at Stony Brook, Inc.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1.\n\n*Provides that the assessor of the town of Brookhaven can accept an\napplication for a property tax exemption from the Chabad at Stony Brook,\nInc. for the 2024-2025 assessment rolls.\n\n*Establishes the enacting clause, Section 2. Sets forth the effective\ndate.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChabad at Stony Brook, Inc's omission to file for tax exemption was an\noversight, one that if recognized earlier, would have been promptly\nrecertified, This technical error should not burden an organization that\nhas consistently contributed positively to the community.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
